())"] [89 16 "// its class"] [94 17 "// its own memory, else nil (a base's, an address's)"] [95 17 "// b_base"] [97 17 "// b_objects"] [99 2 "// a function pointer's state (PyCFuncPtrObject)"] [105 1 "// withFn gives a function pointer instance its PyCFuncPtrObject state (one made from memory: a result, a field)."] [113 1 "// obj is c as a Python object (its class's instance)."] [121 1 "// cdataOf is the CData of o (a ctypes instance), or nil."] [151 23 "// ctypes.ArgumentError"] [160 1 "// _ctypes_simple_instance: true for a subclass of c_int and the like (its base is not _SimpleCData), false for"] [161 1 "// c_int itself (callproc.c: such a class is kept as an instance, not converted by its getfunc)."] [166 1 "// tpName is a type's tp_name as CPython prints it in these messages (its __name__ for a heap type)."] [169 1 "// newCData is generic_pycdata_new / PyCData_MallocBuffer: a zeroed instance of t of its own memory."] [182 1 "// baseKind is the built-in base of a ctypes class."] [193 1 "// fromBaseObj is PyCData_FromBaseObj: an instance of t on base's memory at adr (base nil: a copy of adr's bytes)."] [211 1 "// atAddress is PyCData_AtAddress: an instance of t over the memory at buf."] [222 1 "// container is PyCData_GetContainer."] [248 1 "// keepRef is KeepRef."] [262 1 "// cdataGet is PyCData_get."] [275 1 "// cdataSetInner is _PyCData_set."] [317 1 "// cdataSet is PyCData_set."] [326 1 "// extendError is _ctypes_extend_error: the exception err re-raised as cls with prefix and \"ExcType: msg\"."] [339 1 "// ---- the metatypes ----"] [341 1 "// newClass is type.__new__ for a metatype's class."] [356 1 "// simpleTypeNew is PyCSimpleType_new and PyCSimpleType_init."] [395 2 "// the swapped variant for the byte orders (__ctype_be__, __ctype_le__), as PyCSimpleType_init's create_other_endian_type"] [417 1 "// makeSwapped is create_other_endian_type: a class of the same name with the byte-swapped accessors."] [442 1 "// fmtOf is the buffer format of a simple type's code (_ctypes_alloc_format_string_for_type)."] [463 1 "// structTypeNew is PyCStructType_new/init (and UnionType's): the class, its StgInfo copied from its base's, its"] [464 1 "// _fields_ laid out when given."] [492 1 "// updateStginfo is PyCStructUnionType_update_stginfo: the layout by ctypes._layout.get_layout, then the fields made"] [493 1 "// descriptors of the class (MakeAnonFields included)."] [597 2 "// the aggregate's ffi type (a union: its largest member's elements, stgdict.c's rule, as one struct)"] [619 1 "// makeAnonFields is MakeAnonFields: the fields of each _anonymous_ field's type made the class's, at their offsets."] [647 1 "// makeFields is MakeFields: descr's type's fields as fields of t at offset."] [670 1 "// structTypeSetAttr is PyCStructType_setattro: _fields_ assigned lays the class out."] [689 1 "// arrayTypeNew is PyCArrayType_init."] [743 2 "// char and wchar_t arrays: value and raw"] [757 1 "// pointerTypeNew is PyCPointerType_new/init."] [775 1 "// pointerSetProto is PyCPointerType_SetProto: the item type, and the item type's __pointer_type__."] [791 1 "// funcPtrTypeNew is PyCFuncPtrType_new/init: _argtypes_, _restype_, _flags_."] [841 1 "// converters is converters_from_argtypes: each argtype's from_param."] [857 1 "// ---- CDataType's methods (on the metatypes) ----"] [910 3 "// CPython shares the buffer's memory; a Python buffer's bytes are Go memory, not the C world's: from_buffer"] [911 3 "// copies them (a write through either is not seen by the other: the class :ctypes-buffer-share)"] [1019 1 "// arrayFromCtype is PyCArrayType_from_ctype: the class \"NAME_Array_N\", cached."] [1038 1 "// ---- CField ----"] [1157 1 "// ---- instances ----"] [1159 1 "// simpleNew and genericNew are the types' tp_new."] [1199 1 "// structInit is Struct_init: positional arguments to the fields in order (the bases' first), keywords by name."] [1234 1 "// fieldNamesMRO: the names of the _fields_ of t and its bases, the bases' first (_init_pos_args)."] [1284 1 "// ---- arrays ----"] [1341 1 "// Slice_ is a slice's resolved indices."] [1418 1 "// ---- pointers ----"] [1481 1 "// ---- module functions ----"] [1503 1 "// CArgObject: byref's result, and from_param's."] [1506 15 "// the value's bytes (a pointer: 8)"] [1507 15 "// kept alive"] [1509 15 "// a struct by value: its address"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[123 41] [287 31] [300 38] [333 25] [370 26] [372 35] [401 46] [404 47] [407 47] [410 48] [420 61] [423 58] [475 23] [483 47] [484 42] [554 23] [584 49] [594 24] [604 29] [640 55] [655 66] [663 49] [675 22] [679 47] [736 12] [736 38] [767 44] [783 48] [784 57] [799 37] [808 40] [820 39] [825 52] [890 35] [923 28] [927 36] [952 35] [981 34] [1021 31] [1142 27] [1143 20] [1144 28] [1210 41] [1220 48] [1227 38] [1253 35] [1295 34] [1324 26] [1359 14] [1359 24] [1365 14] [1365 24] [1372 12] [1372 22] [1395 78] [1395 99] [1402 51] [1443 45] [1447 32] [1484 21] [1487 20] [1494 21] [1497 20] [1527 12] [1527 19]]} (go/file "ctypes.go" :imports [

    ;; Modules/_ctypes/_ctypes.c and stgdict.c: Copyright (c) the Python Software Foundation, under the PSF License
